      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Andrew Woods",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>This appears to be directly related to the issue mentioned in this thread (<a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Aa87220be-211e-4d98-b12f-0e772d9888c2\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:a87220be-211e-4d98-b12f-0e772d9888c2\" data-account-id=\"557058:a87220be-211e-4d98-b12f-0e772d9888c2\" accountid=\"557058:a87220be-211e-4d98-b12f-0e772d9888c2\" rel=\"noreferrer\">David Chandek-Stark (old account)</a>)<br/>\n<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/fedora-tech/2MIgi-i6HPU/-H3ZmyilBwAJ\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://groups.google.com/d/msg/fedora-tech/2MIgi-i6HPU/-H3ZmyilBwAJ</a></p>\n\n<p>===========<br/>\nThe main issue I think is that requests to binaries under versions do not include the Link: &lt;uri&gt;; rel=\"describedby\" header.</p>\n\n<p>Here's the header when I GET the binary node URI:</p>\n\n<p>Link: &lt;<a href=\"http://localhost:8983/fedora/rest/dev/8f/49/84/e2/8f4984e2-5fbc-4e6f-bbc1-6b392b580f2a/content/fcr:metadata\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8983/fedora/rest/dev/8f/49/84/e2/8f4984e2-5fbc-4e6f-bbc1-6b392b580f2a/content/fcr:metadata</a>&gt;; rel=\"describedby\"</p>\n\n<p>When I request the binary URI under a version (<a href=\"http://localhost:8983/fedora/rest/dev/8f/49/84/e2/8f4984e2-5fbc-4e6f-bbc1-6b392b580f2a/fcr:versions/87a0a8c317f1e7e3193515-7815-4475-8950-95698c75d2e1/content\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8983/fedora/rest/dev/8f/49/84/e2/8f4984e2-5fbc-4e6f-bbc1-6b392b580f2a/fcr:versions/87a0a8c317f1e7e3193515-7815-4475-8950-95698c75d2e1/content</a>), the describedby link is absent, although the correct info under the predicate <a href=\"http://www.iana.org/assignments/relation/describedby\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.iana.org/assignments/relation/describedby</a> exists at </p>\n{version_uri}\n<p>/fcr:metadata.</p>\n\n<p>I imagine this is what drives the HTML UI to redirect to /fcr:metadata for the non-versioned URI, but not for the versioned URI.<br/>\n===========</p>",
     "created": "04/Apr/16 10:04 AM",
     "id": "16446",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11860/comment/16446",
